WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.400
This is the code that runs behind the demo.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:12.800
Four Rust crates, a React frontend, and the specification it was built from.

3
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:19.700
Types first. No database, no network, nothing to install to test it.

4
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.700
This is a Claim. Every sentence in a report is one.

5
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:32.800
It cannot be built without a source label and a quote from that source.

6
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.700
So a sentence with no evidence behind it cannot be written down at all.

7
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:44.700
This is how the application reaches storage.

8
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.800
Six methods. There are two implementations: Postgres, and one in memory.

9
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:57.300
Every test uses the memory one, so the tests need nothing running.

10
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.700
The queue is a column in the database, not a separate service.

11
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:10.800
Skip locked lets several workers claim jobs at once without collisions.

12
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.600
One fewer thing to run, and one fewer thing to pay for.

13
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.600
A finished report today contains nothing.

14
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.500
It says so, and lists what it would have checked. Same as a real gap.

15
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:33.900
The reading pipeline is next. The shape it fills is already here.

16
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:40.700
This test checks that a failure never shows a reader our internals.

17
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.900
It asserts a database password cannot appear in a response.

18
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:52.300
Two commands to run it. Nothing else to install.

19
00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:58.200
Twenty-seven tests, no database, no keys, no accounts.
